From 8c9aebcdd9f46f7a14b98d6ab18574b7a48fbb08 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: David Rosca <david.rosca@amd.com>
Date: Thu, 30 Jul 2026 17:37:44 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] drm/amdgpu: Reject UVD message with dimensions above 4096
Git-commit: 8c9aebcdd9f46f7a14b98d6ab18574b7a48fbb08
Patch-mainline: v7.2
References: CVE-2026-80908 bsc#1279627

Fixes potential overflow in DPB size calculations.

Signed-off-by: David Rosca <david.rosca@amd.com>
Acked-by: Leo Liu <leo.liu@amd.com>
Reviewed-by: Ruijing Dong <ruijing.dong@amd.com>
Signed-off-by: Alex Deucher <alexander.deucher@amd.com>
(cherry picked from commit 05e1387d151f71569fbe122d2c89f9db0c21dc10)
Cc: stable@vger.kernel.org
Signed-off-by: Gabriel Krisman Bertazi <krisman@suse.de>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/amdgpu_uvd.c |    4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/amdgpu_uvd.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/amdgpu_uvd.c
@@ -528,8 +528,8 @@ static int amdgpu_uvd_cs_msg_decode(stru
 	unsigned image_size, tmp, min_dpb_size, num_dpb_buffer;
 	unsigned min_ctx_size = ~0;
 
-	/* Reject invalid dimensions to prevent division by zero */
-	if (width < 16 || height < 16) {
+	/* Reject invalid dimensions */
+	if (width < 16 || height < 16 || width > 4096 || height > 4096) {
 		dev_WARN_ONCE(adev->dev, 1,
 			      "Invalid UVD decoding dimensions (%dx%d)!\n",
 			      width, height);
